IMPORT `ref-record`

§ `Nine coverage questions put to the record encoding`

-- STANDING PREAMBLE, applied to every claim below:
--   "Assuming all other conditions are met and no other exclusions apply
--    (where by 'other,' I mean anything not referenced in the query that
--    follows)"
-- So every field a query does not touch is set to the value that makes the
-- policy apply, and only the fields the query names are set from the query.
--
-- The favourable baseline is:
--   signed TRUE; premium paid TRUE;
--   a wellness visit in month 3, for yourself, with a qualified provider;
--   written confirmation in month 4, in writing, from that provider
--     (so the 1.3 condition is SATISFIED in a timely fashion);
--   no disclosure defaults;
--   hospitalization in month 3, age 41, all four 2.1(1)-(4) origins FALSE;
--   no dispute or disagreement;
--   written proof of claim in month 4, seeking to recover in month 7.

§§ `Reusable favourable 1.3 facts`

`a good wellness visit` MEANS `Wellness visit` WITH
    `months from the effective date to the visit` IS 3
    `the visit was for yourself` IS TRUE
    `the medical provider was qualified` IS TRUE

`a good written confirmation` MEANS `Written confirmation` WITH
    `months from the effective date to when it was supplied to us` IS 4
    `it is in writing` IS TRUE
    `it is from the medical provider in question` IS TRUE

§§ `Q1 -- burns suffered on duty as a fire fighter`

-- Referenced: the hospitalization was caused by burns suffered while doing
-- duty as a fire fighter. So 2.1(3)'s origin fact is TRUE and the basis is
-- accidental injury. Everything else favourable.
`Q1 firefighter burns` MEANS Claim WITH
    `this agreement had been signed by the time of the hospitalization` IS TRUE
    `the applicable premium for the policy period had been paid by the time of the hospitalization` IS TRUE
    `the wellness visit` IS JUST `a good wellness visit`
    `the written confirmation` IS JUST `a good written confirmation`
    `disclosure defaults` IS EMPTY
    `the hospitalization on which the claim is premised` IS Hospitalization WITH
        `months from the effective date to the hospitalization` IS 3
        `your age in years at the time of the hospitalization` IS 41
        `the basis of the hospitalization` IS `accidental injury`
        `the event causing it arose directly or indirectly out of skydiving` IS FALSE
        `the event causing it arose directly or indirectly out of service in the military` IS FALSE
        `the event causing it arose directly or indirectly out of service as a fire fighter` IS TRUE
        `the event causing it arose directly or indirectly out of service in the police` IS FALSE
    `the dispute or disagreement, if any` IS NOTHING
    `months from the effective date to the submission of written proof of claim` IS JUST 4
    `months from the effective date to when you seek to recover` IS 7

#EVAL `a benefit is payable on this claim` `Q1 firefighter burns`

