§§ `Q9 -- bitten in the ankle by your son; a serving police officer`

-- Referenced: basis (a bite from one's son is accidental injury); the
-- confirmation was supplied at month 6, inside 1.3's month-7 deadline; and You
-- were serving as a police officer at the time of the hospitalization.
--
-- 2.1(4)'s operative fact is not "You are a police officer" but "the event
-- causing the sickness or accidental injury arose directly or indirectly out
-- of service in the police". The query states an employment status at the time
-- of the hospitalization and supplies no causal link at all between police
-- service and a son's bite, so that fact is FALSE. The sensitivity run below
-- shows what the encoding says on the opposite reading.
`Q9 son bit my ankle, a serving officer` MEANS Claim WITH
    `this agreement had been signed by the time of the hospitalization` IS TRUE
    `the applicable premium for the policy period had been paid by the time of the hospitalization` IS TRUE
    `the wellness visit` IS JUST `a good wellness visit`
    `the written confirmation` IS JUST (`Written confirmation` WITH
        `months from the effective date to when it was supplied to us` IS 6
        `it is in writing` IS TRUE
        `it is from the medical provider in question` IS TRUE)
    `disclosure defaults` IS EMPTY
    `the hospitalization on which the claim is premised` IS Hospitalization WITH
        `months from the effective date to the hospitalization` IS 3
        `your age in years at the time of the hospitalization` IS 41
        `the basis of the hospitalization` IS `accidental injury`
        `the event causing it arose directly or indirectly out of skydiving` IS FALSE
        `the event causing it arose directly or indirectly out of service in the military` IS FALSE
        `the event causing it arose directly or indirectly out of service as a fire fighter` IS FALSE
        `the event causing it arose directly or indirectly out of service in the police` IS FALSE
    `the dispute or disagreement, if any` IS NOTHING
    `months from the effective date to the submission of written proof of claim` IS JUST 4
    `months from the effective date to when you seek to recover` IS 7

#EVAL `a benefit is payable on this claim` `Q9 son bit my ankle, a serving officer`

